# The generated INSERT SQL holds real customer, order and financial data.
# It must never enter git. run.py deletes each file as it loads; this is the
# guard for when a run is interrupted.
sql/
*.sql

# ...except the hand-written Postgres survey, which is an input.
!survey_pg.sql

# Every report the scripts write. Regenerate by re-running the script.
*.log
*.json
!plan.json
# copy_order.json was here until 2026-08-21. run.py now DERIVES the order at
# run time from plan.json and SQLite's foreign keys, so there is no stored
# order to commit. The exception is removed rather than left dangling: if a
# file by that name reappears it is a run artefact and should stay ignored.
# run.py writes copy_order_used.json -- the order a run ACTUALLY used, kept
# as evidence on the output side, and ignored here like every other output.

__pycache__/
